{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .agents/skills/knowledgehub-import/SKILL.md'","aggregated_output":"---\nname: knowledgehub-import\ndescription: Interpret an explicitly selected design and working UI source package into a fresh native KnowledgeHub model, with exact sources, typed definitions, recoverable publication and independent coverage verification.\n---\n\nUse a local execution-capable agent host with the current knowledgehub-model\nbinary. Read the supplied package's ownership hierarchy before modelling, then\nread [the native tool contract](references/model-authoring.md). Use the [exact JSON example](references/authoring-example.json) when authoring\nconfig/host/plan/coverage files; its four object members are separate input files.\nObtain explicit\nsource, new destination, private run directory, scope and current host authority.\nIf local execution or the matching catalogue is unavailable, report that unmet\nprerequisite; do not simulate an import.\n\nInventory every supplied file, exact original digest, media, authority, duplicate\nrendition, local dependency and exclusion. The designated working UI is design\ncontent, irrespective of its directory name. Analyse HTML/CSS/scripts, controls,\nstates, confirmations, errors, permissions, command effects and assets as data.\nKeep binary originals separate from supplied extraction/locator artifacts.\n\nCreate a reviewable typed plan and independent source obligation/query inventory.\nUse actual catalogue tokens and native kernel variants. Preserve stable source\nidentifiers, shared story placements/cuts, direct lifecycle subjects, logical\napplication targets, inherited schemas and honest planned realization. Add no\napplication-specific built-in ontology types. Source-bound narrative/Body and\nartifacts can retain detail beyond structured formalization; state that limit.\n\nResolve material source conflicts with an authorized person when their input is\nneeded; otherwise retain exact conflicting support and an unresolved decision.\nAgent interpretation is not human review. Simulated research remains simulated;\nabsent implementation, accounts, provider actions and application tests remain\nabsent. Do not invent defaults or use gaps to excuse malformed supplied values.\n\nRun catalogue -> capture -> prepare -> assess -> create with explicit files and\ncurrent host inputs. Before reporting completion, invoke the independent\n[knowledgehub-verify workflow](../knowledgehub-verify/SKILL.md). Structural\ncompleteness cannot replace source coverage. Report every unexhausted query,\nunsupported item, source gap and unresolved interpretation.\n\nAfter interruption preserve the run and destination. Use resolve, then same-run\nresume. Never reset stores, edit accepted backend files, change original intent,\nor use a new operation ID to bypass uncertainty or denial. Source changes require\na new reviewed run and fresh destination. Respect the user's authorized scope.\n\nReturn native directory, scope, exact head, baseline, catalogue/profile,\nsource/mapping/coverage artifacts and known receipts. Separate source coverage,\nnative validity/completeness, interpretation review, implementation evidence and\nhuman acceptance. For a reproducible example read\n[the fixture walkthrough](references/fixtures.md).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
